|name2 = Grandiose Gunhauzer
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Grandiose Gunhauzer''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
Grandiose Gunhauzer is an [[:Category:Anti-Zombie Cats|anti-Zombie]]/[[:Category:Anti-Aku Cats|Aku]] crowd-controller with relevant immunities. It has a phenomenal pierce of up to 740 range through its [[Explosion]], but its [[Freeze]] activation rate sits at only 50%, making it generally unreliable in pivotal moments. Grandiose Gunhauzer's matchups are generally better suited against [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombies]] than [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]] due to its lack of [[Shield Piercing]], limiting it to [[Shield|unshielded]] Aku unless you also bring a [[:Category:Shield Piercing Cats|Shield Piercer]]. Even against Zombies, however, it still doesn't fare too well as quicker Zombies like [[Zory]] and [[Zang Roo]] tend to burrow during its long attack cycle. Additionally, its [[Conjure]] ability, despite the spirit having [[Zombie Killer]] and [[Soulstrike]], still hinders it, as said spirit lacks any crowd-control effects, and being a [[:Category:Cats with Conjure ability|Conjure unit]], Gunhauzer cannot be stacked, being limited to one instance of it active at any given moment. Its most notable use is to finish off low-HP threats when Z-Killing is uncertain, such as in mixed stages.

Despite this, Grandiose Gunhauzer's HP and knockback count are enough to tank enemy ambushes. Its uptime—should Freeze choose to activate—is at a comfortable 90% against Zombies, and 75% against Aku, taking into consideration the Explosion ability. [[Immune to Toxic|Toxic Immunity]] gives it a good matchup against [[Big Peng Z]] and [[Zollow]], and occasionally helps against [[Oldstrich]]. So, while finicky, Grandiose Gunhauzer is ultimately a good crowd-controller, but shouldn't be relied on too heavily.

