==Trivia==
*Mighty Morta-Loncha appears to be a foil to [[Mighty Kat-A-Pult (Uber Rare Cat)|Mighty Kat-A-Pult]]:
**Mighty Morta-Loncha is best described as a counterweight trebuchet, a siege weapon designed to launch objects over large distances not unlike a catapult. However, it uses a weighted lever to propel its payload at a high vertical trajectory, rather than strictly laterally.
**The cosplaying cat dons an identical set of gladiator gear, and assumes the same pose seen in Mighty Kat-A-Pult. But unlike the latter, this cat is seen actively contributing to the machine's operations.
**They both attack with a giant boulder.
**Their Evolved Forms operate transforming tank-like vehicles fueled by coal. However, where CAT-6 Siege Engine attacks with multiple explosive artilleries lined throughout the entire contraption, Grandious Gunhauzer engages targets with just the main cannon.
*The mustachioed cat that appears in all of the other [[Frontline Assault IRON LEGION (Gacha Event)|IRON LEGION]] units is the spirit conjured by Mighty Morta-Loncha.
*In [[The Battle Cats|English version]], Mighty Morta-Loncha was created to oppose an ancient empire, but in the [[Nyanko Daisensou|Japanese version]], it was created by said empire.

